    q: 'What is congenital adrenal hyperplasia?',
    a: 'Congenital adrenal hyperplasia (CAH) is a group of inherited conditions in which the adrenal glands lack an enzyme needed to make cortisol. In the great majority of cases the missing enzyme is 21-hydroxylase. Without cortisol the pituitary keeps sending ACTH, which enlarges the adrenals and pushes them to overproduce androgens.',
