    q: 'What newer treatments target the ACTH signal itself?',
    a: 'Two approaches. Crinecerfont, approved by the FDA in December 2024, blocks the CRF1 receptor at the pituitary so less ACTH is released. An investigational drug, atumelnant, blocks MC2R at the adrenal so the gland cannot respond to ACTH; it is in a Phase 3 trial and is not approved.',
